    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d438">

                <pb facs="0666" n="566" xml:id="pg566"/>

                <head>No. 438.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Heap
                        to Mr. Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1884-06-04"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 4, 1884</date>.
                        (Received June 23.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 396.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: * * * A note was sent to me on the 2d
                    instant by the minister for foreign affairs, reminding me that the treaty of
                    commerce would cease to exist on the 5th of June, I enclose a copy of this
                    communication as well as of my reply to it dated to day, informing his
                    excellency that in the view of the Government of the United States the treaty of
                    1882 is <hi rendition="#italic">not</hi> duly ended, but if the Imperial
                    Government maintains its intention of denouncing that treaty, I am instructed to
                    declare to his excellency that the United States Government falls back on the
                    treaty concluded in 1830, which remains in full force and effect in all its
                    parts after the expiration of the treaty of 1862. * * *</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>G. H. HEAP.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d438-a1.xml" xpointer="d438-a1"/>
